# Every change needs the maintainer's review.
#
# Later rules win in CODEOWNERS, so the catch-all comes first and the
# deliberately-called-out paths follow it.
*                       @AgentCount/maintainers

# ── The two paths where a quiet change is the actual risk ──────────────────
#
# crates/checks is the only place a verdict is formed. Everyone whose agent
# fails a check has an incentive to soften one, so this path is named
# explicitly rather than left to the catch-all — a reviewer should never be
# able to say they did not notice which directory a diff was in.
/crates/checks/         @AgentCount/maintainers

# The schema decides what evidence survives a run. A dropped column is an
# un-recomputable result, and unlike a bad check it cannot be fixed after the
# fact by re-judging the archive.
/migrations/            @AgentCount/maintainers

# The rules a rung-4 verdict cites, and the pinned spec text itself.
/spec/                  @AgentCount/maintainers

# What the project promises about how it measures, and the record of every
# time that promise changed.
/METHODOLOGY.md         @AgentCount/maintainers
/CHANGELOG-METHODOLOGY.md @AgentCount/maintainers

# Governance and licensing.
/LICENSE                @AgentCount/maintainers
/TRADEMARK.md           @AgentCount/maintainers
/GOVERNANCE.md          @AgentCount/maintainers
/.github/               @AgentCount/maintainers
